            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/56/88656/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                "username": "harshit-aghera"
            },
            "createdOn": 1775567898,
            "author": {
                "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                "username": "harshit-aghera"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuDevice.cpp",
                    "line": 146,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Master already has the LONG_RUNNING_RESPONSE event registration from 88160.\nAfter rebasing, will this patch combine both EventDescriptors into a single initializer_list, like the following?\n```\n  eventReporting = std::make_shared<NvidiaEventReportingConfig>(\n      eid, mctpRequester,\n      std::initializer_list<EventDescriptor>{\n          {gpu::MessageType::DEVICE_CAPABILITY_DISCOVERY,\n           static_cast<uint8_t>(\n               gpu::DeviceCapabilityDiscoveryEvents::LONG_RUNNING_RESPONSE),\n           std::bind_front(&NvidiaLongRunningResponseHandler::handler,\n                           longRunningHandler)},\n          {gpu::MessageType::PLATFORM_ENVIRONMENTAL,\n           static_cast<uint8_t>(gpu::PlatformEnvironmentalEvent::XID),\n           std::bind_front(&NvidiaXidEventHandler::handleXidEvent,\n                           xidEventHandler)}});\n```\nbuildEventSourceMasks already handles multiple descriptors across different message types, so they should coexist."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuDevice.cpp",
                    "line": 146,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuMctpVdm.cpp",
                    "line": 1144,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: Could we replace this magic number `3` with a named constant or\nadd a brief comment? It took me a moment to figure out what these\n3 bytes correspond to.\n\nPer the NSM spec, the XID event payload is structured as:\n\n    struct nsm_xid_event_payload {\n        uint8_t  flag;            // 1 byte\n        uint8_t  reserved[3];     // <- this skip(3)\n        uint32_t reason;          // 4 bytes\n        uint32_t sequence_number; // 4 bytes\n        uint64_t timestamp;       // 8 bytes\n    } __attribute__((packed));\n\nSo the `3` here is the `reserved[3]` field (alignment padding before\n`reason`). Something like the following would make this self-documenting:\n\n    constexpr size_t xidEventReservedBytes = 3;\n    buffer.unpack(flags);\n    buffer.skip(xidEventReservedBytes);\n    buffer.unpack(eventMessageReason);\n\nOr alternatively, just a one-line comment:\n\n    buffer.skip(3);  // reserved[3] padding before reason (NSM XID event payload)\n\nEither works for me \u2014 whichever you prefer. Thanks!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuMctpVdm.cpp",
                    "line": 1144,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuXid.cpp",
                    "line": 40,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "NvidiaLongRunningResponseHandler validates eventInfo.eventClass before processing. \nShould XID events do the same?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuXid.cpp",
                    "line": 40,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "`Event Class` value of XID event is not specified by the spec."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuXid.cpp",
                    "line": 47,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: messageTextString points into the input buffer.\nConsider std::string instead."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuXid.cpp",
                    "line": 47,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "It's intended since it is not being used outside this function."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuXid.cpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eric Liu",
                        "email": "liuer@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "liuer-sys"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: would you mind making the type explicit here, just to match the\npattern used in the other GPU files (GpuDevice, NvidiaGpuMemoryDevice,\nInventory, etc.)?\n\n    std::shared_ptr<NvidiaXidEventHandler> self = weak.lock();\n\nThanks."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuXid.cpp",
                    "line": 74,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuXid.cpp",
                    "line": 84,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "Should every XID event be logged as Critical (e.g., XID 13, XID 31)?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuXid.cpp",
                    "line": 84,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuXid.cpp",
                    "line": 85,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Create is now deprecated:\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-logging/blob/master/README.md#deprecated-methods-for-creating-event-logs\n\nThe preferred approach is to define the event in PDI YAML and use lg2::commit(EventClass(...)). This also avoids encoding metadata into the message string, which is discouraged by:\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/anti-patterns.md#ill-defined-data-structuring-in-lg2-message-strings\n\nIf we still want to use this API, could the XID number, sequence, etc. be passed via additionalData using REDFISH_MESSAGE_ID / REDFISH_MESSAGE_ARGS so bmcweb can map this to a Redfish event registry entry?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuXid.cpp",
                    "line": 85,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "This app does not use bindings generated from PDIs, so we can't use lg2::commit. bmcweb does not use REDFISH_MESSAGE_ID / REDFISH_MESSAGE_ARGS to pick the registry."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/tests/test_NvidiaGpuSensorTest.cpp",
                    "line": 3130,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: After Eric's suggestion on the magic 3 in decodeXidEvent is applied, this 20 should be derived from the same named constants in NvidiaGpuMctpVdm (e.g., sum of the field sizes), or share a single xidEventHeaderSize constant."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/tests/test_NvidiaGpuSensorTest.cpp",
                    "line": 3130,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
